It is a psalm that shows how relationships work.

491
01:30:37.906 --> 01:30:44.906
It is a psalm that shows how God thinks about you and what He wants for you.

492
01:30:44.906 --> 01:30:47.906
God wants you to be happy.

493
01:30:47.906 --> 01:30:49.906
God wants you to be healthy.

494
01:30:49.906 --> 01:30:52.906
God wants you to be successful.

495
01:30:52.906 --> 01:30:55.906
God wants you to have peace in your heart.

496
01:30:55.906 --> 01:30:58.906
God wants you to bear fruit.

497
01:30:58.906 --> 01:31:02.906
Bearing fruit means being successful.

498
01:31:03.906 --> 01:31:08.906
When I read this psalm, I thought to myself, bam, that's it, I don't need to read further.

499
01:31:08.906 --> 01:31:15.906
Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked.

500
01:31:15.906 --> 01:31:20.906
What I just showed you, my context of my own life, has a lot to do with this.

501
01:31:20.906 --> 01:31:23.906
For me, my repentance was about friendships.

502
01:31:23.906 --> 01:31:28.906
I had to walk away from friendships that would not lead me to Jesus.

503
01:31:28.906 --> 01:31:34.906
Psalm 1. Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked.

504
01:31:34.906 --> 01:31:41.906
Who does not stand in the way of sinners.

505
01:31:41.906 --> 01:31:44.906
Nor sits in the seat of scoffers.

506
01:31:44.906 --> 01:31:56.906
Yes, but Tim, I sit at the table of scoffers because I have a job in a company, and when it's break time at ten in the morning and they are at the boat ramps, they talk about, do you have any?

507
01:31:56.906 --> 01:32:01.906
And then they talk about this and that, those are things you just don't say on this stage.

508
01:32:01.906 --> 01:32:04.906
And this is the talk of the break at your work.

509
01:32:04.906 --> 01:32:11.906
And you think to yourself, the one who does not sit at the table of scoffers, how should I deal with this?

510
01:32:11.906 --> 01:32:16.906
But you went very differently. I'm not saying you should go eat your sandwich somewhere else.

511
01:32:16.906 --> 01:32:24.906
But I do say, just as Jesus was not influenced by the prostitute, but the prostitute was influenced by Jesus.

512
01:32:24.906 --> 01:32:29.906
So you can be an influence in the lives of this table.

513
01:32:29.906 --> 01:32:44.906
We are obviously talking here about sitting at the table with scoffers to have friendship with them and thinking that your influence may come from these related people.

514
01:32:44.906 --> 01:32:46.906
Do you understand what I mean at home?

515
01:32:47.906 --> 01:32:49.906
Verse 2.

516
01:32:49.906 --> 01:33:00.906
But blessed is the man who finds joy in the law of the Lord and meditates on his law day and night.

517
01:33:00.906 --> 01:33:02.906
One of my key Bible verses.

518
01:33:02.906 --> 01:33:07.906
Immerse yourself in the laws of God day and night.

519
01:33:07.906 --> 01:33:10.906
You don't have to read the Bible day and night.

520
01:33:10.906 --> 01:33:14.906
You should read your Bible at a certain part of the day.

521
01:33:14.906 --> 01:33:19.906
Even if it's just one verse a day, be occupied with it.

522
01:33:19.906 --> 01:33:24.906
Be alert to those few words you have read and be engaged with them.

523
01:33:24.906 --> 01:33:32.906
Maybe you can handle reading an entire letter from the New Testament at once with your brain capacity.

524
01:33:32.906 --> 01:33:35.906
With Titus, that's a bit easier than with Romans.

525
01:33:35.906 --> 01:33:41.906
But maybe you can handle reading one of the prophets at once with your brain capacity.

526
01:33:41.906 --> 01:33:42.906
Then do that.

527
01:33:42.906 --> 01:33:45.906
But be alert to what the Word of God says.

528
01:33:45.906 --> 01:33:51.906
For it says here that you meditate day and night on the laws of God.

529
01:33:51.906 --> 01:33:54.906
He will be, and here it comes.

530
01:33:54.906 --> 01:33:57.906
You may underline this in your Bible.

531
01:33:57.906 --> 01:34:03.906
Just underline, He will be like a tree planted by flowing water.

532
01:34:03.906 --> 01:34:05.906
This is what God wants from you.

533
01:34:05.906 --> 01:34:07.906
In due time, He bears fruit.

534
01:34:07.906 --> 01:34:11.906
Not on your time, but in His time, He bears fruit.

535
01:34:11.906 --> 01:34:13.906
His leaves do not wither.

536
01:34:13.906 --> 01:34:14.906
You do not need to be afraid.

537
01:34:14.906 --> 01:34:16.906
God will not let you fall.

538
01:34:16.906 --> 01:34:18.906
Everything He does comes to fruition.

539
01:34:18.906 --> 01:34:22.906
For God has placed His breath of life in you.

540
01:34:22.906 --> 01:34:25.906
So if you engage with Him, there is life in you.

541
01:34:25.906 --> 01:34:27.906
Verse 4.

542
01:34:27.906 --> 01:34:30.906
You may underline this verse 3.

543
01:34:30.906 --> 01:34:31.906
Why?

544
01:34:31.906 --> 01:34:35.906
I do not want to be a preacher who only delivers stern sermons.

545
01:34:35.906 --> 01:34:39.906
I also want to be a preacher who shows that God has a promise for your life.

546
01:34:39.906 --> 01:34:43.906
I want to be a preacher who shows that God loves you.

547
01:34:43.906 --> 01:34:45.906
He has a hopeful future for you.

548
01:34:45.906 --> 01:34:47.906
He wants to make you happy.

549
01:34:47.906 --> 01:34:51.906
He is joy, humor, life, strength, victory.

550
01:34:51.906 --> 01:34:53.906
This is God.

551
01:34:53.906 --> 01:34:56.906
And He wants you to be like Him.

552
01:34:56.906 --> 01:34:58.906
This is my God.

553
01:34:59.906 --> 01:35:01.906
But I also want to be honest,

554
01:35:01.906 --> 01:35:03.906
that if I say something that the Bible says,

555
01:35:03.906 --> 01:35:06.906
and if the Bible then says, but we will approach it this way,

556
01:35:06.906 --> 01:35:08.906
you must also say that.

557
01:35:08.906 --> 01:35:11.906
The way to blessings is through obedience.

558
01:35:13.906 --> 01:35:16.906
Verse 4.

559
01:35:17.906 --> 01:35:19.906
But it is not so with the wicked.

560
01:35:19.906 --> 01:35:21.906
Honesty is delightful.

561
01:35:21.906 --> 01:35:22.906
And this is one.

562
01:35:22.906 --> 01:35:28.906
They are like chaff that blows away in the wind.

563
01:35:28.906 --> 01:35:32.906
The lawless do not stand where justice prevails.

564
01:35:32.906 --> 01:35:36.906
Sinners do not belong in the circle of the righteous.

565
01:35:38.906 --> 01:35:39.906
Do you see it?

566
01:35:39.906 --> 01:35:42.906
In the circle of the righteous, sinners have nothing to seek.

567
01:35:43.906 --> 01:35:45.906
They have nothing to relate to each other.

568
01:35:46.906 --> 01:35:48.906
Hey Tim, go out with me one more time.

569
01:35:48.906 --> 01:35:51.906
Some time ago, there was someone I happened to see again

570
01:35:51.906 --> 01:35:53.906
and they said, come, go with me to such a party one more time.

571
01:35:54.906 --> 01:35:55.906
And I said, I have nothing to seek there.

572
01:35:55.906 --> 01:35:57.906
Really, I have nothing more to seek there.

573
01:35:57.906 --> 01:36:02.906
I would, I would not belong there anymore, I no longer fit in there.

574
01:36:05.906 --> 01:36:07.906
The lawless do not stand where justice prevails.

575
01:36:07.906 --> 01:36:09.906
Sinners do not belong in the circle of the righteous.

576
01:36:09.906 --> 01:36:10.906
Verse 6.

577
01:36:10.906 --> 01:36:14.906
The Lord protects the way of the righteous.

578
01:36:14.906 --> 01:36:18.906
The way of the lawless leads to ruin.

579
01:36:19.906 --> 01:36:20.906
Ruin.

580
01:36:22.906 --> 01:36:23.906
Verse 4.

581
01:36:23.906 --> 01:36:25.906
They are like the chaff that blows away in the wind.

582
01:36:25.906 --> 01:36:26.906
Verse 4.

583
01:36:26.906 --> 01:36:29.906
They are like the chaff that blows away in the wind.

584
01:36:30.906 --> 01:36:34.906
Like a farmer bringing in his grain, separating the grain from the chaff.

585
01:36:35.906 --> 01:36:38.906
When a farmer brings in the grain and he has gathered the harvest,

586
01:36:38.906 --> 01:36:41.906
he picks up that grain and throws it into the air.

587
01:36:42.906 --> 01:36:47.906
For that grain, namely those seeds, are heavy and come back down.

588
01:36:47.906 --> 01:36:49.906
But the wind may take the chaff away.

589
01:36:50.906 --> 01:36:52.906
But where does that chaff end up?

590
01:36:53.906 --> 01:36:56.906
Do you know where that concerns the farmer?

591
01:36:56.906 --> 01:36:57.906
Not at all.

592
01:36:58.906 --> 01:37:00.906
For it is not about the chaff.

593
01:37:00.906 --> 01:37:02.906
The chaff does nothing.

594
01:37:03.906 --> 01:37:05.906
Where that chaff lands, who cares?

595
01:37:05.906 --> 01:37:06.906
In the river, on the land.

596
01:37:06.906 --> 01:37:07.906
But it bears no fruit.

597
01:37:07.906 --> 01:37:11.906
The chaff that falls to the ground does not produce new grain.

598
01:37:11.906 --> 01:37:13.906
That chaff dies.

599
01:37:13.906 --> 01:37:14.906
The chaff is already dead.

600
01:37:14.906 --> 01:37:16.906
Only it was first mixed with the grain.

601
01:37:17.906 --> 01:37:19.906
At some point, it needs to be shaken up.

602
01:37:20.906 --> 01:37:22.906
Maybe there are people in the church.

603
01:37:23.906 --> 01:37:28.906
You come year in, year out, you come to church, out of religion, out of tradition.

604
01:37:29.906 --> 01:37:31.906
And maybe you need to wake up.

605
01:37:31.906 --> 01:37:33.906
Maybe you are chaff instead of wheat.

606
01:37:34.906 --> 01:37:38.906
I cannot judge that at this moment, because you will soon see a Bible verse,

607
01:37:38.906 --> 01:37:40.906
that it is also not my place to judge.

608
01:37:40.906 --> 01:37:43.906
But you must hold a Bible verse in front of you and say,

609
01:37:43.906 --> 01:37:45.906
am I actually chaff or am I actually wheat?

610
01:37:45.906 --> 01:37:48.906
Am I actually bearing fruit?

611
01:37:49.906 --> 01:37:51.906
Am I something substantial?

612
01:37:51.906 --> 01:37:54.906
Or am I something, and here it comes, what this Bible verse says.

613
01:37:54.906 --> 01:37:56.906
Can we see it one more time?

614
01:37:56.906 --> 01:37:57.906
Verse 4.

615
01:37:57.906 --> 01:38:01.906
They are like the chaff that blows away in the wind.

616
01:38:01.906 --> 01:38:07.906
I want to show you something that strikes me very strongly about this society we are currently living in.

617
01:38:07.906 --> 01:38:09.906
This society moves quickly.

618
01:38:09.906 --> 01:38:12.906
What is in fashion today is no longer in fashion tomorrow.

619
01:38:12.906 --> 01:38:15.906
Even if you were to renovate your house today and think to yourself,

620
01:38:15.906 --> 01:38:18.906
oh that looks nice, white walls and black lamps, that is really super cool.

621
01:38:18.906 --> 01:38:19.906
Tomorrow it won't be cool at all.

622
01:38:19.906 --> 01:38:22.906
Oh yes, that was so 2020, in 2021 they say.

623
01:38:22.906 --> 01:38:24.906
So it goes so fast.

624
01:38:24.906 --> 01:38:26.906
Everything goes so super fast.

625
01:38:26.906 --> 01:38:31.906
Today they are releasing a new model car and tomorrow they are releasing yet another new model car.

626
01:38:31.906 --> 01:38:35.906
Today we find this in our ethical norms and values.

627
01:38:35.906 --> 01:38:38.906
And tomorrow we find it completely different.

628
01:38:39.906 --> 01:38:41.906
And this is the wind and the chaff.

629
01:38:41.906 --> 01:38:44.906
Can you picture it? I can visualize it so well.

630
01:38:44.906 --> 01:38:48.906
And there stands the farmer throwing the grain and the chaff into the air.

631
01:38:48.906 --> 01:38:51.906
And the wind does what it wants.

632
01:38:51.906 --> 01:38:53.906
The wind goes everywhere.

633
01:38:53.906 --> 01:38:56.906
And away goes the chaff.

634
01:38:56.906 --> 01:38:58.906
Where does it go? Who knows?

635
01:38:58.906 --> 01:39:01.906
Does it have a purpose then? No, it has no purpose.

636
01:39:01.906 --> 01:39:02.906
Chaff has no purpose.

637
01:39:02.906 --> 01:39:04.906
Chaff may go.

638
01:39:04.906 --> 01:39:06.906
No interest in chaff.

639
01:39:07.906 --> 01:39:14.906
Imagine if you were to be guided by the influences of the wind.

640
01:39:14.906 --> 01:39:22.906
Imagine this world with the morality that this world has today.

641
01:39:22.906 --> 01:39:31.906
Imagine that the world may influence you in terms of relationships.

642
01:39:31.906 --> 01:39:38.906
Where are your relationships going, and more importantly, where is your life headed?

643
01:39:38.906 --> 01:39:41.906
Where do you end up then?

644
01:39:41.906 --> 01:39:43.906
That is the point of that chaff.

645
01:39:43.906 --> 01:39:45.906
Where does it ultimately end up?

646
01:39:45.906 --> 01:39:47.906
I don't know.

647
01:39:47.906 --> 01:39:50.906
The purpose of all this separating of wheat and chaff.

648
01:39:50.906 --> 01:39:54.906
The intention is that the substantial returns.

649
01:39:54.906 --> 01:39:56.906
So that the farmer can do something with it.

650
01:39:56.906 --> 01:39:59.906
He can make bread from it or he can reseed it.

651
01:39:59.906 --> 01:40:00.906
He needs to know that.

652
01:40:00.906 --> 01:40:02.906
But it has a purpose.

653
01:40:02.906 --> 01:40:04.906
God has a purpose for your life.

654
01:40:04.906 --> 01:40:07.906
God has an intention for your life.

655
01:40:07.906 --> 01:40:11.906
God does not want you to fly away like that chaff at some point.

656
01:40:11.906 --> 01:40:12.906
And who knows?

657
01:40:12.906 --> 01:40:14.906
There isn't even a check anymore.

658
01:40:14.906 --> 01:40:16.906
There is no farmer who ultimately looks.

659
01:40:16.906 --> 01:40:17.906
Ah, there it goes.

660
01:40:17.906 --> 01:40:19.906
No, there is work to be done.

661
01:40:19.906 --> 01:40:23.906
So you don't want to end up on the ground aimlessly.

662
01:40:23.906 --> 01:40:25.906
And this is very much Psalm 1.

663
01:40:25.906 --> 01:40:27.906
For verse 6 says indeed.

664
01:40:37.906 --> 01:40:42.906
Why does David start with this Bible verse?

665
01:40:42.906 --> 01:40:46.906
Why does David start with Psalm 1 regarding this whole question?

666
01:40:46.906 --> 01:40:50.906
Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked.

667
01:40:50.906 --> 01:40:53.906
That's how verse 1 begins.

668
01:40:53.906 --> 01:41:00.906
In some way, David has also written this down as a life lesson for himself.

669
01:41:00.906 --> 01:41:03.906
This is what I should not do.

670
01:41:03.906 --> 01:41:08.906
For if I associate with the lawless, I apparently do not find happiness in that.

671
01:41:08.906 --> 01:41:10.906
The Bible verse says indeed.

672
01:41:15.906 --> 01:41:18.906
People at home, about relationships.

673
01:41:18.906 --> 01:41:21.906
You will be happy in your relationships.

674
01:41:21.906 --> 01:41:27.906
If you do not approach it the way the whole world is approaching it right now.

675
01:41:27.906 --> 01:41:30.906
You will be happy in your life.

676
01:41:30.906 --> 01:41:35.906
If you say, Lord, what your Word says about my life, that is truth.

677
01:41:35.906 --> 01:41:38.906
What your Word says about relationships, that is truth.

678
01:41:38.906 --> 01:41:43.906
What your Word says about entering into a relationship with the Father.

679
01:41:43.906 --> 01:41:47.906
Why do we call the Creator of heaven and earth Father?

680
01:41:47.906 --> 01:41:54.906
Because we can relate to Him as someone who protects, who provides.

681
01:41:54.906 --> 01:41:57.906
Therefore we call him Father.

682
01:41:57.906 --> 01:42:00.906
Do you know what Jesus says about God?

683
01:42:00.906 --> 01:42:02.906
Father.

684
01:42:02.906 --> 01:42:05.906
Jesus was a human, just like you and me.

685
01:42:05.906 --> 01:42:11.906
Jesus was just as human as you are human.

686
01:42:12.906 --> 01:42:15.906
Jesus was not less human.

687
01:42:15.906 --> 01:42:20.906
A little less human, so that there was also a little more divinity in Jesus.

688
01:42:20.906 --> 01:42:25.906
Jesus was not 50% human and 50% God.

689
01:42:25.906 --> 01:42:30.906
Jesus was 100% human.

690
01:42:30.906 --> 01:42:35.906
The Bible says that Jesus had to learn obedience.

691
01:42:36.906 --> 01:42:41.906
The Bible says that Jesus was not pre-programmed to obey.

692
01:42:41.906 --> 01:42:45.906
Jesus was indeed 100% human.

693
01:42:45.906 --> 01:42:47.906
With free choice.

694
01:42:47.906 --> 01:42:49.906
To make choices about who he associated with.

695
01:42:49.906 --> 01:42:52.906
To make choices about who could influence him.

696
01:42:52.906 --> 01:42:55.906
To make choices about who he called Father.

697
01:42:55.906 --> 01:43:02.906
Jesus was 12 years old and he says, I had to be about my Father's business.

698
01:43:03.906 --> 01:43:06.906
Jesus continuously calls God Father.

699
01:43:06.906 --> 01:43:11.906
Why? Because Jesus and God had something related to each other.

700
01:43:13.906 --> 01:43:18.906
I want to arrange my friendships, as I mentioned earlier, together with Vanessa.

701
01:43:18.906 --> 01:43:22.906
that my friendships are those people who may influence me.

702
01:43:22.906 --> 01:43:27.906
People may influence me from whom I see that they also have something to say.

703
01:43:27.906 --> 01:43:30.906
For here is my lesson that I have also learned.

704
01:43:30.906 --> 01:43:35.906
Initially, I had written down for myself, friendships influence.

705
01:43:35.906 --> 01:43:39.906
And influences become decisions. That is my other lesson.

706
01:43:39.906 --> 01:43:42.906
An influence always becomes a decision.

707
01:43:42.906 --> 01:43:45.906
An influence always becomes a decision.

708
01:43:45.906 --> 01:43:48.906
Influences lead to decisions.

709
01:43:48.906 --> 01:43:55.906
You cannot be influenced by something and say, I have just taken this in.

710
01:43:55.906 --> 01:43:59.906
I have allowed this into my life, but I will make my decisions completely differently.

711
01:44:00.906 --> 01:44:04.906
You cannot watch certain television programs and say,

712
01:44:04.906 --> 01:44:09.906
yes, I watch that, but I will handle my relationships completely differently.

713
01:44:09.906 --> 01:44:14.906
That won't work. Why? Because God has set you up that way.

714
01:44:14.906 --> 01:44:19.906
He wants you to be a follower. Then be a follower of the good.

715
01:44:19.906 --> 01:44:25.906
So decide at this moment to fill yourself with things that are good for your life.

716
01:44:26.906 --> 01:44:30.906
Proverbs 13 verse 20. To support what I just said.

717
01:44:30.906 --> 01:44:36.906
Proverbs 13 verse 20. If you walk with wise people, you will become wise.

718
01:44:36.906 --> 01:44:43.906
The influences that come into your life, you must choose yourself.

719
01:44:43.906 --> 01:44:47.906
If you walk with wise people, you will become wise.

720
01:44:47.906 --> 01:44:55.906
But if you are friends with fools, and here it comes, it will end badly for you.

721
01:44:55.906 --> 01:45:04.906
You cannot possibly be successful while saying that you relate a lot to fools.

722
01:45:04.906 --> 01:45:08.906
Impossible. Your colleagues are your colleagues.

723
01:45:08.906 --> 01:45:12.906
But they don't have to be your friends who may influence you,

724
01:45:12.906 --> 01:45:16.906
who may give you influence over how you spend your weekend.

725
01:45:16.906 --> 01:45:19.906
Or how you deal with your wife.

726
01:45:19.906 --> 01:45:23.906
I have worked in construction and I have heard things that people say,

727
01:45:23.906 --> 01:45:30.906
about how they handle their relationships, of which I thought, I better not handle my relationships that way.

728
01:45:30.906 --> 01:45:35.906
And by the way, I am also married to someone who would not tolerate that.

729
01:45:37.906 --> 01:45:44.906
If you associate with wise people, you become wise. Do you understand that?

730
01:45:44.906 --> 01:45:49.906
If someone is wise, it rubs off, as they say in English.

731
01:45:49.906 --> 01:45:51.906
It rubs off, it transfers.

732
01:45:51.906 --> 01:45:57.906
So if you are with someone who is smart, and that person is continuously spewing out that smartness, that wisdom,

733
01:45:57.906 --> 01:46:02.906
because out of the abundance of the heart, the mouth speaks.

734
01:46:02.906 --> 01:46:07.906
