02:01:16.906 --> 02:01:19.906
Judge your own relationships.

977
02:01:19.906 --> 02:01:25.906
For I want to conclude with these last words, one more time, from Psalm 1, verse 3.

978
02:01:25.906 --> 02:01:30.906
You will be like a tree, planted by flowing water.

979
02:01:30.906 --> 02:01:34.906
In due time your relationship will bear fruit.

980
02:01:34.906 --> 02:01:37.906
Your leaves will not wither.

981
02:01:37.906 --> 02:01:40.906
And everything you want to experience in a good relationship,

982
02:01:40.906 --> 02:01:44.906
will flourish in the mighty name of Jesus.

983
02:01:44.906 --> 02:01:46.906
I will see you all next week.

984
02:01:46.906 --> 02:01:49.906
This coming Wednesday there is the Midweek Update.

985
02:01:49.906 --> 02:01:51.906
Thank you all for watching.

986
02:01:51.906 --> 02:01:56.906
Be engaged with these words, so that you stand strong and powerful in your relationships.

987
02:01:56.906 --> 02:01:59.906
I will see you Wednesday at the Midweek Update.

988
02:01:59.906 --> 02:02:00.906
Bye bye.

989
02:02:01.906 --> 02:02:02.906
Amen.
